WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.200
.

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.640
Just follow along step-by-step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

4
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.520
tablets each

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:17.290
and a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 pm the night

6
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.400
before your procedure.

7
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.800
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

8
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.800
ounces of water

9
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.170
up to the fill line. Swallow one tablet every two minutes with a sip of water,

10
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:30.560
finishing all

11
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.880
12 tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

12
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:43.680
About one hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

13
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.480
of water

14
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.860
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes

15
00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.640
after finishing

16
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.300
that container, fill it one more time with 16 ounces of water and drink the

17
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.960
entire amount over 30

18
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:04.310
minutes. That completes your first dose. Repeat the exact same three steps

19
00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:05.600
using your second bottle

20
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:11.290
of 12 tablets. One tablet every two minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water

21
00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.400
one hour later,

22
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:18.400
then 16 ounces of water 30 minutes after that. This part is really important.

23
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.360
You must drink

24
00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.420
all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already passing clear

25
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.080
liquid.

26
00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:29.040
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

27
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.320
the clearest view

28
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.200
during your procedure. If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to

29
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.560
reschedule and neither

30
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.930
of us wants that. Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to stay hydrated.

31
00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:42.400
It will help

32
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.070
you feel better and help the prep do its job. Do not drink anything at all

33
00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.320
within four hours of

34
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.640
your procedure, including water, unless it is a small sip to take a medication.

35
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:58.560
Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled if this is not followed. If you

36
00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.440
experience any

37
00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:05.680
discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash

38
00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:11.690
cream can really help. That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish

39
00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:12.480
the full dose,

40
00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.030
and stay hydrated. If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our

41
00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:17.520
office.

42
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.420
We're here to help.
